e75cee3a3698794b4b6f5574a8774f0575bc0c21
# ^ The commit the prod image runs (scripts/engine-assets.sh reads the first line;
# this comment is ignored).
#
# NOT an upstream commit as of 2026-08-31. It is upstream `23b9466c` plus two
# patches, carried on https://github.com/brianhliou/pikafish-jieqi-wasm branch
# `jieqi_old-mistboard`, and the Build engines workflow fetches it from THAT repo
# rather than official-pikafish/Pikafish. The upstream base is unchanged, so moving to a newer
# upstream jieqi_old is a cherry-pick, not a merge. The pinned commit must be
# reachable from that branch: the build clones it --single-branch.
#
# e75cee3a (2026-09-03): a Threads.stop check and a main-thread check_time() at
# qsearch entry (src/search.cpp). qsearch had neither, and the dark-piece recursion
# re-enters it at depth 0, so `go movetime` could not stop a thread inside those
# tails and bestmove waited on the slowest helper. Found while root-causing #335.
#
# The patch stops ScoreCalc averaging a forced loss away at dark-piece flip nodes: a
# mate was clamped to +/-DARKVALRATE (2862) and then diluted by the other revealed
# identities, so the engine could score itself comfortably ahead while being mated.
# Measured on 30 mate-decided positions: mates seen behind a dark root move went from
# 39/47 to 44/47, none lost, and 4 of 89 non-mate evals moved (max 50 cp). Rig and raw
# transcripts: mistboard-engine lab/jieqi-darkmove-2026-08-31/.
#
# Pinned 2026-08-28. Before this, the build was `git clone --depth 1 -b jieqi_old`,
# so every deploy rebuilt the analysis engine from whatever branch tip existed that
# day. That is a reproducibility hole with teeth: whole-game analysis is cached by
# (room, engine, depth), and the engine component was a hand-maintained version
# string that knew nothing about the binary. Two deploys either side of an upstream
# commit would therefore file evals from two different engines under one identical
# key, with nothing to detect it. The xiangqi Pikafish build had the same hole
# until 2026-09-23, when pikafish.ref pinned it to the commit production was
# already running.
#
# The short form of this SHA is part of JIEQI_ANALYSIS_ENGINE_ID, so moving this pin
# invalidates jieqi analysis caches on purpose rather than silently reusing them.
# jieqi-engine-ref.test.ts fails if the two drift apart.
#
# Bumping: check out the new ref, rebuild, and expect a full recompute of every
# jieqi review. There is no way to keep the old rows: they were produced by a
# different engine, which is the whole point of keying on this.
#
# The browser WASM analysis build must move WITH this pin, or the analysis board and
# the server run different engines while the articles tell readers they are the same
# one. Its source of truth is apps/web/public/engine/pikafish-jieqi/ (source.patch +
# pikajieqi-source-<short>.tar.gz) and its cache-buster is ENGINE_ASSET_VERSION in
# apps/web/src/review/engine/pikajieqi-ceval.ts.
